E**: if `tasks/CODEX-WALL` exists, read it and obey: NO refills (§2E suspended), NO re-queues of wall-class failures; drains/gates/merges/assayer/bookkeeping/authoring CONTINUE (Claude-side, unaffected). Once per fire, establish whether the implementer is serving — ⚠️ **BUT NOT WITH A BARE `codex` PROBE. THIS CLAUSE PRESCRIBED EXACTLY THAT UNTIL s1640, AND IT IS STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE OF EVER REPORTING A WALL LIFTED (F-1636-4, filed s1636, owed three fires, DISCHARGED s1640).** A fire's bare `codex` resolves to `/opt/homebrew/bin/codex` — `which -a codex` finds **only** that one (re-measured s1640) — and it is **0.133.0**, below the **0.144.1** floor `lane-runner-v3.sh:448` names for knowing 5.6 ids (was `:422` before the s2319 F-2319-1 factory-accounting withhold, +26 lines; `:172` before the s1651 codex-client-floor block, +47 lines — cite the CODE, the coordinate drifts), so a `-m gpt-5.6-sol` probe returns HTTP 400 *"requires a newer version"* **whatever the quota is**. The runner NO LONGER invokes bare `codex` — as of s1651 (F-1651-1) it resolves a client meeting the 0.144.1 floor before consuming a master (`lane-runner-v3.sh:449`, was `:423`, `:340`, `:173`), self-healing past a wrong-shell PATH and refusing loudly rather than shredding the queue. Before that fix it invoked bare `codex` but from Robin's nvm-shimmed Terminal, so **PATH decides and the two shells do not share a binary** — which is why the s1631 wall outlived its cause by ~3 hours. ➡️ **PRIMARY INSTRUMENT — ASK THE ARTIFACT THE FACTORY ACTUALLY PRODUCED. IT COSTS NOTHING AND HAS NO BINARY QUESTION AT ALL: the newest `tasks/runs/*.log` banner.** Every run log opens with `OpenAI Codex v<ver>` + `model: <id>` (verified s1640 against the then-live `20260810-212739` lane-d log: `v0.145.0`, `model: gpt-5.6-sol`). A run whose banner names the model and which does **not** die on a usage-limit message proves the implementer served at that timestamp — which is the entire question the probe was trying to an