or `20` changed files: nine named tracked files, and the entire 11-file evidence directory as the single entry `?? artifacts/e4-roads-and-convoys/`.** ⚠️ **THEREFORE A DIRT COUNT READ FROM `git status` IS A COUNT OF *ENTRIES*, NOT OF FILES, AND THE GAP IS UNBOUNDED — one line can hide any number of files. Our own instrument inherits it: `lane-usable --all` reports `lane-b … untracked=1`, which is CORRECT about entries and is 11 files and 1.0 MB on disk.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOTHING WAS LOST — all 15 are now on `save/lane-inflight-evidence-s2489` (PARENTLESS, so it can never read as a merge candidate), PUSHED to origin, and re-measured `AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0 · SAFE 35 / 35`. This is NOT a false green: no instrument ever claimed these were safe, because none was ever asked, and `lane-usable` never claimed to count files.** 🎯 **What earns it a clause is the DIRECTION plus a loss path that is CODE rather than conjecture: `lane-runner-v3.sh:550` refreshes a lane with `git reset --hard main && git clean -fd`, and **`clean -fd` DELETES UNTRACKED FILES** — so this evidence is ONE refill away from gone, and what protects it today is only the temporary policy fence on `tasks/BACKLOG.md` line 1 (*"no refills into b/d until their leaves flip"*), which lifts at exactly the moment those two tracks finish. The lane-d files are the CONTROLLERS that produce the proof, and the wip commit says *"resume from here"* — a resumed implementer starting from that commit after a `clean -fd` would have to write them again.** ➡️ **THEREFORE, BINDING, AS PART OF THE SAME SWEEP: run `git worktree list` and take the untracked read in **EVERY** registered tree, inside the root as well as outside — the rule’s discriminator is REGISTRATION, never location.** Judge what it returns by the five tests above, salvage with F-2484-1’s untouching method, and **never `git add` into a lane you do not own: a `save/*` ref makes the bytes permanent and decides nothing.** ⓘ **Untouchedness was MEASURED, not trusted — `git status --porcelain` on main and both lanes reads `19/10/1` on BOTH sides.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: an untracked file in a live lane is a LAWFUL, routine mid-run state, so a red would fire during ordinary correct operation and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate) — the same restraint F-2357-1, F-2389-1, F-2484-1, F-2485-1, F-2487-1 and F-2488-1 all took for this very sweep. The cure is the sentence you are reading.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS after F-2484-1 (*which TREE?*), F-2485-1 (*a registry is not a census*) and F-2487-1/F-2488-1 (*how many declared subjects did the author VISIT?*): A SUMMARY VIEW IS A LOSSY PROJECTION, AND `git status` IS ONE. Every prior finding in this streak asked how a subject SET could be wrong; this one has the right set and reads a COLLAPSED VIEW of it. When you count dirt, ask whether your instrument reports FILES or ENTRIES — and if a single line can stand for a directory, it can stand for a megabyte.** 🔢 **AND THAT CLASS IS NOW CENSUSED — IT HAS EXACTLY ONE LIVE MEMBER, THE ONE ALREADY KNOWN, AND THE TWO MOST DANGEROUS DIRT-READERS IN THE FACTORY WERE IMMUNE BY CONSTRUCTION ALL ALONG. THE FINDING IS THE *NEGATIVE*; DO NOT RE-TAKE IT (F-2490-1, measured and cured s2490 by executing the one-fire-old cure against the class its author could not sweep).** 📊 **MECHANISM VALIDATED FIRST RATHER THAN INHERITED (F-2215-1): `--porcelain` vs `--porcelain -uall` on the live trees gives lane-b `7 → 17` and **main itself `26 → 90`, a 3.46× collapse, today**.** ✅ **CENSUS: `lane-runner-v3.sh:11` — the delta committer whose miss CAUSED F-2489-1's near-loss — already passes `--porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all`, and `art-staging-audit.mjs:439`, the RETENTION LAW's own alarm, already passes `--untracked-files=all`. `lane-usable.mjs`'s `dirt()` was the ONLY live member, and there is no second collapse ro