tool could not tell you which corpus its licence came from while its sibling arm had been saying so since s2213.** 🛠️ **CURE: `goalEvidence()` returns `{ source: 'goals' | 'absent', leaves }` — a STRING for F-2212-1's reason — carried in `--json` ALWAYS including the happy path (F-2208-1), with the human channel printing only a DEVIATION to match this file's own `reviewsSource` convention. `absent` DECLARES AND DOES NOT REFUSE (F-2218-1's restraint): a root without `goals.json` is LAWFUL — it is what all 12 legacy fixtures use and how `mainReviews` already treats a non-git root — so refusing there would red every fixture and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1). The parse path is DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE; re-coding a working cure in passing is a drive-by.** ✅ **BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2): all four modes `4/4` byte-identical on stdout and stderr, rc unchanged.** 🔒 **`scripts/master-shipped-goals-source-guard.test.mjs` — 8 tests, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; pre-cure restored verbatim reds 4 of 8 with both reverse controls green.** ⚠️ **A REVERSE CONTROL CORRECTED MY PREDICTION for the first time in three fires: I expected *refusing on `absent`* to red control 5 alone; it reds FOUR arms (2,3,4,5), because arms 2–4 read the absent-state classification a refusal replaces with a banner. Benign — over-coverage, not under — but recorded, because the streak's recent note has been that predictions hold, and one clean fire is not evidence the practice can be dropped.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is an AIMING rule rather than another census shape: A CENSUS'S DECLARED LIMIT IS THE MOST VALUABLE THING IN A HANDOFF — WORTH MORE THAN THE SITE IT NAMES.** s2218 handed over a hedged target (`art-staging-audit.mjs:373`, still unmeasured) *and* an admitted blind spot (*"my census is lexical and single-line"*). **Widening the census on that admission — multi-line guards as well as single-line ones — took its `6` sites to `13` single-line plus `4` multi-line, and found a live one in NEITHER list, because widening changed which FILES were subjects at all, not merely which lines.** When a predecessor tells you what their instrument cannot see, go there before you go to the site they named. ⚖️ **A priced leaf is NOT a closed one** — the tool prints that caveat itself; the price estimates the AUTHORING cost and never renders a verdict on the goal. If the ladder has nothing ready for an idle lane, **AUTHOR the next master yourself** (idle-fire authoring precedent: s41 m3-02, s42 m4-02) — but ONLY from an existing spec slice plus its evidence chain (predecessor's review file, audit verdicts, playtest findings — read them, quote them in the task). Follow the house task pattern (goal / scope / firewall / self-check, gates, sequencing laws), mark the header **FIRE-AUTHORED (attended review welcome)**, max one authored master per fire, no drain-budget cost — ⚖️ AMENDED (owner 2026-08-09, F-1511-5 ruling "Allow 2 masters when dry"): when the board is DRY (no drain existed this fire) and ≥2 lanes sit idle, the cap is TWO authored masters in that cycle; the cap protects quality, not idleness. HARD LIMIT — never invent scope: if the lane's next work has no spec slice, needs a design fork, or bends canon, do NOT author — flag **PIPELINE-DRY: <lane> (needs spec/owner)** in your handoff instead. Refills are non-drain actions (no budget cost). **MAIN THROTTLE (s72 lesson, 2026-07-06): while ≥3 undrained done-moves are waiting, do NOT refill the main queue beyond one small corrective — every main task holds the working tree dirty and blocks ALL lane merges. Drains outrank main throughput; re-queue paused main items (queue-paused/) once the pile is below 2.** 📮 **DISPATCH ORDER IS A LAW, NOT A HABIT — COMMIT THE MASTER AND ITS EVIDENCE FIRST, REFRESH THE LANE SECOND, `cp` THIRD, AND RUN THE MASTER'S OWN CITATION GREP BETWEEN 2 AND 3 (F-1424-3, measured s1424; folded in s1426 after being deferred one fire for a lane collision that has since cleared).** s1424 cured lane-c *before* committing the master, so the lane sat **exactly one commit behind** — the commit carrying the citation the master tells the runner to grep. The runner claimed the slot inside a minute and STOPPED: **44,007 tokens, zero files touched, zero work lost**, saved only because that master wired the grep as a hard STOP. ⚠️ **Curing the message could never have prevented this** — the fault is ordering, and no instrument was being asked about it. ➡️ **AND THE KEY ITSELF MUST BE PROVED BEFORE IT IS WRITTEN DOWN: grep the candidate span against the SOURCE FILE ON MAIN first — if it does not match *there*, it is not a key, it is a paraphrase (F-1425-2).** F-1310-1 says cite by CONTENT because coordinates rot; what neither clause said is that **`grep` is line-oriented and prose wraps**, so a key spanning a line break matches **nowhere, including in the file it was copied from**. s1425 caught this on its own dispatch: the key returned 0 in the lane and its first instinct was a stale lane, but `lane-usable` read `ahead=0 behind=0` and the same grep returned **0 against main too**. That failure is nastier than staleness because **the master specifies 0 to mean "the lane drifted"** — a false STOP whose error message accuses the wrong subject, sending the next fire chasing a phantom refresh. ⓘ **This is not a rare shape: s1426 hit it again while authoring, and all three of its first-draft keys returned 0 on main** — the fire had written the review file itself minutes earlier and its own prose still wrapped. Prefer a span that visibly sits on one line, verify **1 on main**, then verify **1 in the lane** after the refresh, and only then `cp`.\012**GOAL REGISTRATION LAW (owner ruling 2026-07-16): every authored master adds its leaf to `tasks/goals.json` IN THE SAME COMMIT; every drain updates that leaf's status and merge hash IN THE DRAIN COMMIT.** Missing goal-tree bookkeeping means the author/drain duty is unfinished. ⏱️ **AND THE GUARDS THAT JUDGE THAT ROW RUN BEFORE IT EXISTS, SO THEY MUST RUN AGAIN AFTER — `npm run test:ledger-guards`, AS THE LAST ACT OF EVERY FIRE THAT WROTE A LEDGER ROW (F-1300-4, mechanism landed s1301).** This is a property of the prescribed ORDER, not of anyone's carelessness: §3 runs the battery on the MERGED tree, and the merged tree by definition **precedes** the drain-bookkeeping commit — so every guard that reads `tasks/goals.json`, `tasks/BACKLOG.md` or tracked `tasks/**/*.md` evaluates the board **as it was before the fire wrote its own row**. A fire that runs the battery once, exactly as ordered, is therefore **structurally incapable of seeing a defect it is about to introduce**. s1300 wrote `mergeHash: "818aa398"` where `scripts/goal-tracker.test.mjs:80` asserts `/^[0-9a-f]{40}$/`, and `test:node-guards` went **rc=1 on a tree whose code was green**; it was caught only by a re-run that an unrelated edit happened to prompt — luck wearing diligence's clothes. It is the citations-run-LAST rule with a wider denominator. 📋 **The denominator was DERIVED s1301, not inherited — and then WIDENED the same fire when it proved too narrow, which is the more useful half of the story.** First pass asked *which guards read the live LEDGER* and found six: `goal-tracker.test.mjs` (live `goals.json` **and** `tasks/done` — the second source was not in the finding) · `goal-closure-reason.test.mjs` · `ruling-propagation-guard.test.mjs` **and** `ruling-propagation-guard.mjs` · `findings-state-guard.mjs` · `blocker-panel-closed-guard.mjs` · `citation-title-guard.mjs`. ⚠️ **Then s1301's own bookkeeping reddened `test:node-guards` in two ways that those six are blind to** — `gate-caller-audit` (the new npm script was an un-rooted gate) and `law-pointer-guard` (inserting a comment block pushed `workers: isFireShell` from `:30` to `:50`, rotting the coordinate that **this very clause** and `.claude/skills/drain/SKILL.md` both cite). Neither reads the ledger; both were caught only by the full battery