the owner (batch the rest into the weekly roundup item). 🔢 **AND THAT BUDGET IS A *WEEKLY AGGREGATE* THAT NO SINGLE FIRE CAN SEE — SO ASK THE SWEEP, WHICH NOW COUNTS IT FOR YOU, BEFORE YOU FILE (F-2491-1, measured and cured s2491).** A fire files ONE item, for ITS OWN drain, and that act is locally correct **every single time**. The rule's subject is the WEEK, and until this fire nothing in the loop observed it: `gazette-backfill-sweep` counted `reported / dismissed / candidates` and had **no opinion whatever** on how many headlines the week already held. 📊 **MEASURED s2491 for ISO week 2026-W36: `18` standalone items against a budget of `3` — six times over — filed by ELEVEN SEPARATE FIRES (s2459 · s2460 · s2461 · s2462 · s2468 · s2469 · s2470 · s2471 · s2472 · s2473 · s2476), each judging its own merge worth a headline.** ⓘ **Fires DO batch when they think of it — `6` ROUNDUP-CLASS items sit in the very same window, and their own prose says *"the week's three headline slots are spent"* — so this is not neglect. THE COUNTING WAS A HABIT, NOT A STEP**, and during a high-drain burst every fire independently reached the same locally-correct answer. ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOT a false green, nothing is broken, and NO VERDICT ANYWHERE WAS WRONG — every one of those 18 items is honest news about a real merge. The queue is a QUEUE the owner approves FROM, so an over-full queue publishes nothing to the family.** 🎯 **What earns it a clause is the DIRECTION: it fails toward MORE owner load, in the one pipeline whose entire purpose is to BOUND owner load — the owner's "one morning action" is handed 18 headlines to weigh where the rule promises 3.** ➡️ **THE DUTY IS NOW ONE LINE OF THE SWEEP YOU ALREADY RUN: it prints `weekly headline budget (<ISO week>): N standalone, M batched` on EVERY run including the happy path (F-2208-1), and when the slots are spent it names what is already standing so the warning is actionable rather than a scold. 