ess.mjs` avoids `Date` parsing on purpose and says so, which is where this trap was already named for its own two scripts. This was an **ad-hoc triage probe**, the kind a fire types by hand and no battery observes (the F-1582-1 gap). 🎯 **What earns it a clause is the DIRECTION and the UNIFORMITY: the answer is not off by a day, it is `0` for EVERY subject — the empty-corpus false green this file has spent twenty fires curing, arriving through a TIMEZONE rather than a `catch`, a guard, a cwd or a filename. A quiet-day verdict and a 95-commit day are byte-identical, so the probe is right exactly when you are lucky.** ➡️ **THE CURE IS ONE ARM AND IT IS F-2215-1's RULE APPLIED TO A WINDOW RATHER THAN TO A TOOL: before trusting a zero, run the same probe over a day whose count you already know is non-zero. If THAT comes back `0` too, the window is broken, not the day.** 🚫 **No guard is proposed and the restraint is measured: there is no shipped artifact to guard, and "did a fire hand-type a correct date window?" is unobservable to every battery — the same reason F-1669-1 declined a mechanism. This is a READING habit, like §2.0c's runner check.** 💡 **REUSABLE: a corpus can go empty from a TIMEZONE as easily as from a name, a cwd or a stale tree — and a window is a selector nobody in this streak has been keyed to check. Whenever a probe reports "nothing happened", ask what it would have reported had something happened.**\012\012## RT-01 DUTY — the weekly rotation mint (added 2026-09-03, attended — the transfer board's fresh seeds, spec `specs/transfer-board.md` L2/L5)\012ONCE PER ISO WEEK, on the first fire after Sunday 00:00 UTC (check whether `assets/rotations/rotation-seeds.json` already holds the rotation whose `opensAt` is the coming Monday; if yes, DISCHARGE with one line): mint it with `node scripts/rotation-mint.mjs --week <YYYY-Www of the coming Monday> --salt-file ~/.goldrush/rotation-salt --append assets/rotations/rotation-seeds.json`, refresh the fenced block in `public/skill.md` between `skillmd-guard:rotations:start/end` with that rotation's JSON, re-pin the skill.md guard baseline per its own instructions, move `CURRENT_ROTATION_ID` in `site/assay-office.js` to the rotation that is OPEN (not the one just minted), commit path-scoped with prefix `rt:`, push, and note it in the handoff. The salt is owner-held and never committed; a missing salt file is a STOP with one desk line, never a default.\012\012## LB-01 DUTY — the county book's daily offsite pull (added 2026-08-24, attended — l4 follow-up #2)\012ONCE PER COVERAGE DAY (the TK-01 cadence — check whether `artifacts/ledger-backups/` already holds today's `ledger-YYYY-MM-DD.db`; if yes, DISCHARGED, move on): run `node scripts/ledger-backup-pull.mjs`. It is idempotent and bounded; box unreachable = WARN in the handoff, never a red, retry next fire. If it pulled a new file: `git add artifacts/ledger-backups/<file>` path-scoped + commit (`ops: LB-01 ledger mirror <date>`) + push — origin IS the offsite copy (the l4 design: no new secrets on the box). ⚠️ STANDING GATE from the l4 runner's own note: BEFORE the accounts flip onto sqlite, this raw mirror must become an ENCRYPTED artifact — a plaintext ledger of county standings is fine, account data is not. That flip's master must name this line. 🔒 **AND THAT GATE NOW HAS AN INSTRUMENT INSTEAD OF ONLY A SENTENCE — RUN `node scripts/ledger-mirror-exposure.mjs` (F-2353-1, measured and cured s2353).** The gate sat here as PROSE from 2026-08-24 with **zero enforcement surface**, and the manual key-read s2352 added below covers the `--fill-gaps` arm ONLY — so the DAILY arm, the one whose output this duty tells you to `git add` + commit + **push**, had neither an instruction nor an instrument. ⚖️ **NOTHING IS EXPOSED TODAY, measured not assumed: all 6 mirrors hold `kv` only, 32 keys, ZERO account-class rows.** 🚪 **What earns it a tool is that the door is ONE-WAY: a committed account row can only be undone by a history rewrite, i.e.