 5 on 08-29, anchored on `^[fire-runner] .*FIRE START`); 35 of them ran, found a decapitated factory, and did not notice — 37h50m dead. Their logs carry ZERO mentions of `health-watch`, `start-lane-runner`, `runner : DEAD` or `runner_pids`.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: the realised cost was ZERO. The board was dry throughout — 0 queued, 0 in-flight, 0 fire-authorable — so nothing was starved, no drain was missed, and every DRY verdict those 35 fires published was TRUE.** This is not a false green about work that existed; it is an instrument that cannot tell a factory AT REST from a factory that CANNOT RUN. 🎯 **WHAT EARNS IT A CLAUSE IS THE DIRECTION AND THE ARMED TRAP: §2E's dry-board allowance lets a fire author up to TWO masters and `cp` them into a lane queue — and with no runner they would sit there forever while EVERY prescribed §2F instrument kept reporting health.** `dry-board-probe` reads `tasks/done/` and says DRY (correct — a queued master is not a done-move); `lane-usable` reads branches and says USABLE (correct); `tasks/running/` is empty (correct, and it is the *symptom*); and `authorable-candidates` would report FEWER planned leaves, because queueing flips them out of `planned` — **so the board would look MORE worked the instant it became incapable of working.** 🔁 **This is the known sibling one level worse: a LIVE runner refusing a queued master at least writes a refusal per poll cycle (s2257: `e10s-1c-ember-shore-inert-landing`, 5h15m, 1,100 logged refusals, and the prescribed cure is `grep -c "REFUSE <name>" logs/runner-headless.log`). A DEAD runner writes NOTHING, and that cure's own trigger — a non-empty queue beside an empty `tasks/running/` — is STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE of firing here, because on a dry board the queue is empty too.** ➡️ **THEREFORE, BINDING, AS PART OF §2 TRIAGE ON EVERY FIRE: run `bash scripts/health-watch.sh status` — two seconds, one screen — and READ THE `runner :` LINE.** It prints `ALIVE` or