h a green suite attesting to it, so arm 6 asserts a hand-edited lane still reads `tracked-dirt=1` / `DIRTY`.** ⚠️ **AND ARM 6 PASSED VACUOUSLY ON ITS FIRST WRITING, WHICH IS THE METHOD LESSON OF THIS FIRE: routing `git()` through `repoRoot()` RECURSES (`repoRoot` → `tryGit` → `git` → `repoRoot`…), so the manufactured defect died on a stack overflow and the arm went green having tested NOTHING. The tell was WALL TIME — 11.5 s against ~200 ms for every other arm — not any assertion. It now resolves the forced root up front and asserts the variant produced output and classified the lane before reading its verdict. A control whose defect arm CRASHES is F-2215-1's silence wearing a different costume: assert the arm RAN, and treat an outlier duration as a defect report.** 💡 **REUSABLE, AND IT RETIRES THE KEY MY PREDECESSOR HANDED ME: s2220 aimed the next fire at a one-grep census over all 326 scripts for the TOKEN `process.cwd()`. That key is ANTI-CORRELATED WITH THE DEFECT AND SCORES ZERO ON BOTH FILES s2220 ITSELF CURED — measured s2221 against the pre-cure blobs, `nul-audit.mjs` **0** occurrences, `attended-owed-audit.mjs` **0**; the occurrences in those files TODAY were ADDED BY THE CURE. Across the corpus the token appears in `7.3%` of files with an implicit corpus root versus `8.7%` of the rest: no discriminating power at all.** 🔭 **WHY, and this is the durable half: CWD-DEPENDENCE IS THE DEFAULT — it is written by SAYING NOTHING (a bare relative path, a spawn with no `cwd` option). The token `process.cwd()` marks an author who THOUGHT about the root, so it tags the SAFER population. Ask instead HOW THE CORPUS GETS ITS ROOT — anchored (`import.meta.url` / an absolute constant / a git-resolved root) versus IMPLICIT. Measured on that key: `96` of `326` non-test scripts have an IMPLICIT corpus root.** ⓘ **A NEGATIVE RESULT BANKED WITH ITS MECHANISM (F-2214-1), because it is a live thread and the obvious reading of it is wrong: `scripts/collection-guards-cwd-invariance.