s an ANSWER and not a failed read): `30` answered · `0` could-not-answer · `5` hold untracked content · `35` paths under an evidence prefix, of which **`15` were in NO object database** — the gate logs, tapes and summaries of `lane-b/artifacts/e4-roads-and-convoys/` (11 files, 1.0 MB) and the CONTROLLERS of `lane-d/artifacts/e8-mare-claim-physics/` (`prover.mjs`, `ride.mjs`, `probe-seams.mjs`, `probe-threats.mjs`).** 🔑 **AND THE CAUSE IS A MEASURED MECHANISM, NOT NEGLECT — THIS IS THE HALF TO CARRY: both lanes carry an attended `wip:` commit reading *"work in progress salvaged attended during the API outage (uncommitted edits of the interrupted implementer; resume from here)"*, and BOTH commits contain ONLY tracked-file edits — `0` `artifacts/` paths between them.** The salvage was careful and path-scoped and still left the evidence behind, because **`git status --porcelain` in `lane-b` prints `10` LINES for `20` changed files: nine named tracked files, and the entire 11-file evidence directory as the single entry `?? artifacts/e4-roads-and-convoys/`.** ⚠️ **THEREFORE A DIRT COUNT READ FROM `git status` IS A COUNT OF *ENTRIES*, NOT OF FILES, AND THE GAP IS UNBOUNDED — one line can hide any number of files. Our own instrument inherits it: `lane-usable --all` reports `lane-b … untracked=1`, which is CORRECT about entries and is 11 files and 1.0 MB on disk.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOTHING WAS LOST — all 15 are now on `save/lane-inflight-evidence-s2489` (PARENTLESS, so it can never read as a merge candidate), PUSHED to origin, and re-measured `AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0 · SAFE 35 / 35`. This is NOT a false green: no instrument ever claimed these were safe, because none was ever asked, and `lane-usable` never claimed to count files.** 🎯 **What earns it a clause is the DIRECTION plus a loss path that is CODE rather than conjecture: `lane-runner-v3.sh:550` refreshes a lane with `git reset --hard main && git clean -fd`, and **`clean -fd`