r a megabyte.** 🔢 **AND THAT CLASS IS NOW CENSUSED — IT HAS EXACTLY ONE LIVE MEMBER, THE ONE ALREADY KNOWN, AND THE TWO MOST DANGEROUS DIRT-READERS IN THE FACTORY WERE IMMUNE BY CONSTRUCTION ALL ALONG. THE FINDING IS THE *NEGATIVE*; DO NOT RE-TAKE IT (F-2490-1, measured and cured s2490 by executing the one-fire-old cure against the class its author could not sweep).** 📊 **MECHANISM VALIDATED FIRST RATHER THAN INHERITED (F-2215-1): `--porcelain` vs `--porcelain -uall` on the live trees gives lane-b `7 → 17` and **main itself `26 → 90`, a 3.46× collapse, today**.** ✅ **CENSUS: `lane-runner-v3.sh:11` — the delta committer whose miss CAUSED F-2489-1's near-loss — already passes `--porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all`, and `art-staging-audit.mjs:439`, the RETENTION LAW's own alarm, already passes `--untracked-files=all`. `lane-usable.mjs`'s `dirt()` was the ONLY live member, and there is no second collapse route (`git ls-files --others --directory` appears **0** times in the repo).** ⚠️ **THE OBVIOUS KEY IS ANTI-CORRELATED, AND THIS IS THE HALF TO CARRY: `--short` scores 6 hits of which **5 are `git rev-parse --short HEAD`** — a different flag entirely, short HASH not short STATUS — while `--porcelain` scores `git worktree list --porcelain`, a different COMMAND, and `desk-state-audit.mjs`'s hit is a JavaScript property named `status`. A token sweep here is mostly false positives; the key is the CALL SITE, read.** That is F-2221-1's `process.cwd()` lesson on a new token, for the second time in this streak. ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: the VERDICT was never wrong — `untracked` is DISPLAY-ONLY (`lane-usable.mjs:505`, `:511`) and drives nothing — so no lane was ever wrongly frozen or wrongly refilled, and this is NOT a false green.** 🎯 **What earns the cure is that `clean -fd` deletes FILES, so the file count is the only number that answers *"what would a refill destroy?"* — the exact question F-2489-1's 1.0 MB was one command away from being answered wrongly.** 💰 **CURED with one flag, PRICED rather than feared: +14% on this tool's git time fleet-wide (19.3s → 22.0s). Reporting BOTH numbers was priced and REJECTED at +50% (+10.4s) for a read every fire runs at triage — and the entry count is the defective number nobody needs.** 📐 **DELTA MEASURED, NOT CLAIMED NEUTRAL, because this cure is deliberately NOT behaviour-neutral (F-1274-2 governs the measurement, not the outcome): across the tool's own 30-row fleet **`0` ahead/verdict values move** and `3` untracked counts become truthful — **lane-b `1 → 21`, the F-2489-1 victim itself** — summing `5` entries → `43` files (8.60×); across the wider 99-tree registry the same call moves `12` trees, `215` entries → `3,925` files (18.26×), worst `gr-task-rehearsal` reading `untracked=4` for **2,738** real files.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/lane-usable-untracked-files-guard.test.mjs` — 9 arms, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`, `gate-caller-audit` PASS. TEETH, 5 variants on scratch copies with the subject restored byte-identical each time: PRE-CURE verbatim reds 4 · `-unormal` reds 3 · the over-general `--ignored` reds its OWN reverse control ALONE · the LAWFUL short form `-uall` correctly stays GREEN · broken git args red 7.** ⚠️ **TWO METHOD NOTES PAID FOR IN THIS FIRE, both caught by controls rather than by reading, and both are new silencers for traps this file already names. (1) A MANUFACTURED VARIANT MUST SATISFY ITS SUBJECT'S OWN MODULE-MAIN PREDICATE: `lane-usable.mjs:622` is a REGEX ON THE FILENAME (`/(^|\/)lane-usable\.mjs$/`), so a variant written as `.tmp-variant-xxx.mjs` never runs `main()` and exits **rc=0, 0 B stdout, no stderr** — indistinguishable from a subject that reported nothing. That is F-2215-1's silent-control trap with a new silencer: there a `/tmp` symlink, here a FILENAME. Name your variant what the subject expects, and copy its relative imports beside it. (2) MY FIRST REVERSE CONTROL ASSERTED THE WRONG BUCKET AND MISSED THE OVER-GENERAL CURE ENTIRELY: git prints ignored paths as `!! path`, and `classifyDirt` sorts only `??` into `untracked`, so `!!` falls through to the TRACKED bucket — **the bucket that DRIVES the DIRTY verdict**. The over-general `--ignored` cure was therefore WORSE than it looked (on the four `*-salvage` trees it would add 10,043 files of lawful build output, F-2486-1) and the obvious control was blind to it. Assert the bucket that has TEETH, not the one your finding is named after.** 🚫 **NO BOARD GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: untracked files in a live lane are a lawful routine state (F-1460-1). What IS guarded is our own CODE — a one-token flag that looks like a redundant default and whose removal is SILENT in every other channel, which is F-1667-1's lesson that an un-annotated cure can undo itself.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS after F-2358-1 (*how WIDE is the selector?*), F-2389-1 (*can the axis EXPRESS the defect?*) and F-2487-1/F-2488-1 (*how many declared subjects did the author VISIT?*): **A CENSUS FRAMED ON A TOKEN FINDS THE WRONG POPULATION; FRAMED ON THE CALL SITE IT FINDS THE RIGHT ONE AND IS DECIDABLE BY READING.** And bank the NEGATIVE loudly — the answer here is *"the class is a singleton and your two most dangerous readers were already correct"*, which is worth exactly as much as a cure and which no future fire should have to re-derive.** 🧾 **AND ASK THE THIRD QUESTION NEITHER OF THOSE READS CAN EXPRESS — `node scripts/withheld-evidence-audit.mjs [--list]` — BECAUSE THE RUNNER ANNOUNCES ITS OWN EVIDENCE LOSSES OUT LOUD AND NOTHING HAS EVER READ THEM (F-2477-1, measured and cured s2477).** `lane-runner-v3.sh` commits a lane's DELTA, so a path already dirty in the lane's baseline is not that run's to claim: it withholds it and logs `[lane-runner-v3] withheld baseline-dirty path: <path>`, once per path. **That refusal is CORRECT for source and INVERTED for `artifacts/**` evidence — there it drops the run's own evidence on the floor