ES to do something, its refusal is a signal with an owner; ask who reads it.** **Report them, do not merely trust them — this audit has now shipped a false zero TWICE, both times because its headline was narrower than the question printed above it. (F-1054-1, fixed s1054 `4051bf31`): it checked only whether a staging file's NAME was absent from main, so 36.54 MB whose name matched main but whose BYTES were in no object database read as `0 files`; it now classifies by blob hash. (F-1055-1, fixed s1055 `c8034384`): "in git" was `cat-file -e`, which asks only THIS disk — so the same 36.54 MB, sitting on a local-only salvage branch whose push had timed out, again read `AT RISK 0`; every in-git blob is now also checked against the remote-tracking refs. If you find a third such gap, fix the class, not the instance.** 🕳️ **AND THE THIRD GAP WAS FOUND — IN THE CURE FOR THE THIRD FALSE ZERO, WHERE THE INSTRUCTION ABOVE SAYS TO LOOK (F-2216-1, measured and cured s2216 — the THIRTEENTH consecutive fire to find a live instance of F-2204-1's class).** The audit's step 2b — F-1184-5's cure, which asks `git diff origin/main..main -- assets/` for assets committed to main and never pushed — sat behind a **bare `catch`** justified by a comment reading *"no origin, or no origin/main remote-tracking ref yet — nothing to compare against, and a missing remote is already the loudest possible signal."* ⚠️ **BOTH HALVES ARE MEASURABLY FALSE, and the first one is the catch's OWN NAMED CASE: it fires when the REMOTE IS PRESENT and only the `origin/main` REF is unavailable — and then `offsite` is still populated from the other remote-tracking refs (137 on this repo), so NOTHING is loud. The unpushed files simply never enter `scan` and appear in no bucket at all.** It fires for any other failure of that one call too, which the comment never contemplated — F-2212-1's class exactly: a handler correct for its named cause and blind to every other one. 📊 **PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING on a scratch repo whose ground truth was ONE unpushed asset. Healthy git: `LOCAL-ONLY 1 files`, names it, `--strict` **rc=1**. Delete only `refs/remotes/origin/main`, remote and other refs intact: `LOCAL-ONLY 0 files`, `--strict` **rc=0**, `--json` `localOnlyFiles: 0` — ALL THREE MACHINE CHANNELS byte-identical to a genuinely safe board. Same for a transient failure of that one call.** The only dissent was an unlabelled line of **git's own stderr**, which no caller classifies and `--json` drops entirely — so per F-2211-1 it is not a signal, it is noise that happens to be true. ⚖️ **SEVERITY, STATED HONESTLY: on the live board the call SUCCEEDS, so every `LOCAL-ONLY 0` this streak has reported was TRUE — verified, not assumed. The defect is that the instrument is structurally incapable of telling you when it stops being true, and its consumer is not a gate but THIS LAW: the ART-SLOT duty makes every dry-board fire report that number to the OWNER, and seven consecutive fires have now reported it.** 🎯 **AND IT BEARS DIRECTLY ON AN OPEN DESK ITEM: F-2159-1 asks whether to root `art-staging-audit --strict` in `test:ledger-guards`. Answering YES before this cure would have rooted an arm that greens on its own blindness — a gate certifying the one thing it cannot see.** 🛠️ **CURE: DECLARE THE SOURCE'S COVERAGE, exactly as F-2196-1 declares the scan's BOUNDARY forty lines up in the same file — the corpus supplied the pattern for the FIFTH fire running. `mainTreeSource` is a STRING for F-2212-1's reason (a careless truthiness test on a failure value is TRUE, i.e. toward declaring), it discriminates `absent-ref` from `unverifiable` because those name two different owed acts (fetch/push vs investigate), it is printed on stdout **ALWAYS — including the happy path** since a declaration that appears only on failure re-creates the very ambiguity it removes (F-2208-1; the §4 desk-header precedent: if the desk is genuinely empty, still write the header), it is carried in `--json`, and `--strict` now separates **2 = "could not answer"** from **1 = "answered, and the answer refuses"** — the convention `drain-block-check`, `dry-board-probe`, `master-shipped-classifier` and `review-evidence-audit` already carry. **The advisory default still exits 0 by design, and this does NOT root the audit's `--strict` in any gate: F-2159-1 is the owner's question and a cure must not prejudge it.**  ✅ **BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2): stdout byte-identical but for the one new declaration line, rc unchanged in both modes, `AT RISK 0 · LOCAL-ONLY 0 · SALVAGED 797 files 600.08 MB`. Per F-2215-1 the control asserted its OWN validity first — "pre-cure arm produced 43 lines, it really ran" — because a control whose failure mode is silence cannot be told from the silence it measures.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/art-staging-local-only-source-guard.test.mjs` — 6 tests, 2.8 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; pre-cure reds 3 of 6, and each over-general cure is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it (collapsing 1 into 2 → arm 1 · declaring only on failure → arm 5 · refusing unconditionally → arms 1 and 6).** ⓘ **AND FOR THE FIRST TIME IN FIVE FIRES THE REVERSE CONTROLS DID NOT CORRECT MY PREDICTION — all four manufactured defects reddened exactly the arms I predicted. Recorded because the streak's running note has been the opposite; one clean prediction is not evidence the practice can be dropped, it is one data point against four.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the census question turned on a different axis: s2215 retired *"what does the TRY contain?"* in favour of *"what does the HANDLER do?"* — LOUD vs SILENT. That is right, and it found this site. But the polarity test is per-HANDLER while the harm is per-CONSUMER, and this handler has BOTH polarities at once: the same swallow makes `AT RISK` bigger (loud, self-announcing) and `LOCAL-ONLY` smaller (silent, a false zero). A handler is not sound because SOME caller notices; ask which number the LAW tells a fire to REPORT, 