guards` leg answers files, leaves and legs in one command — and re-state them here when you do.** 💡 **THE REUSABLE HALF, AND IT IS THIS FACTORY’S MOST-REPEATED FINDING FOR THE SEVENTH TIME WITH A GENUINELY NEW TWIST (F-2153-1 · F-2204-1 · F-2350-1 · F-2360-1 · F-2365-1 · F-2403-1): in all six prior instances the cure’s author did not know which surface governed the moment it applied. HERE THE AUTHOR NAMED THE SURFACE, IN WRITING, INSIDE THE FINDING ITSELF** — s2413 wrote *“this battery is the mandated last act of every ledger-writing fire, so a fire budgeting its closing minutes off ‘seconds’ under-budgets by ~40 s at the worst possible moment”* — **and then landed the number in `tasks/BACKLOG.md` and a guard comment (`61c47292c` touches exactly two files, neither of them a law surface), leaving this clause citing `49.9 s` and “still seconds”. The gap is not KNOWLEDGE, it is that “paste it into the surface that states the duty” is a step no checklist contains. When your finding’s own severity sentence names a reader, THAT SENTENCE IS THE EDIT INSTRUCTION — make the edit before you write the handoff, in the same commit as the measurement.** ⓘ **It is a MINUTE AND A HALF, not a second battery** (this sentence read *“It is still seconds”* from s2099 until s2414 — **RESTATED, not deleted**: it was TRUE at 49.9 s, and it is how a reader was mispriced for ~315 fires) ⏱️ ⛔ **THE `~3 MINUTES` THRESHOLD BELOW IS RETIRED AS A HANG TEST — s2479 MEASURED A FULLY GREEN `436.6 s` RUN, SO "PAST 3 MINUTES" NOW FIRES ON HEALTHY BATTERIES AND ITS DIRECTION IS TO KILL WORKING WORK AND REPORT A GREEN YOU NEVER GOT (F-2479-2). 🚨 WORSE, THE PRESCRIBED DIAGNOSTIC RETURNED THE HANG SIGNATURE ON THAT HEALTHY RUN: the `node`-routed `ps` this clause sends you to look for a 0%-CPU child gave runner `0.36 s` CPU and its child `0.05 s`, BOTH FLAT across a 6-second and a 40-second window — because a process blocked on NETWORK I/O is indistinguishable, by CPU, from one wedged in `uv_thread_join`. 