iminator, `ancestryOfMain`, exits 1 on its refusal and is DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE: re-coding a working cure in passing is a drive-by. The sibling `tasks/done` arm is cured in the same commit (fix the CLASS, not the instance) but declares only when it could NOT read — that corpus is TRACKED and feeds an advisory warn, not a refusal, and an always-on line there is the noise that decays a declaration into a formality. ✅ **BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2): `202` real cases on the live board — leaf-resolved `--queue`, the drain arm, `--all`, `--all --strict` and the no-leaf UNKNOWN path — `202/202` byte-identical on stdout, stderr and rc, with all three verdict arms genuinely reached (`55` CLEAR · `143` refusal · `2` UNKNOWN).** ⚠️ **THE FIRST NEUTRALITY RUN WAS NEARLY VACUOUS AND ITS GREEN WAS WORTHLESS, WHICH IS WORTH MORE THAN THE CURE: it reported `52/52` IDENTICAL while exercising ZERO leaf-resolved `--queue` cases, because `taskFile` values in `goals.json` are BARE BASENAMES and my existence filter tested them as `tasks/…` paths, silently selecting nothing.** The arm I had just changed was never run. **F-2213-1's rule is not optional — CHECK WHAT YOUR FIXTURES MAKE REACHABLE BEFORE TRUSTING WHAT THEY ATTEST — and the tell was arithmetic, not intuition: I expected ~132 cases and got 52.** **When a control's case count does not match what you constructed, the control is selecting something other than what you think.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/dispatch-corpus-guard.test.mjs` — 8 tests, 0.8 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; the pre-cure file restored verbatim reds 5 of 8 with BOTH reverse controls green.** ⚠️ **Each over-general cure is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it, and by nothing else: refusing on `absent` reds 3 and is caught ONLY by *"an absent corpus must NOT refuse"* · declaring unconditionally reds EXACTLY 1, caught ONLY by *"a genuinely clear board says nothing extra"* · collapsing 2 into 1 reds exactly 1 · moving the declaration