ch-number holds still.** 📈 **All 29 new masters registered = 100.0%**, up from 98.0% (s1538→s2100) and 93.3% (s1276→s1538) — the Registration Law is working *better* each window, and the debt is inert legacy decaying purely by dilution, exactly as F-1538-1 predicted and this clause restated. **Re-measure the ABSOLUTE, not the ratio; carry the trigger forward unchanged.** ⓘ **METHOD CONTROLLED AGAINST THREE HISTORICAL TREES BEFORE ANY DRIFT WAS ASSERTED — WIDENED TO FIVE s2182, ALL REPRODUCED TO THE DIGIT** (s1276 `527/763 = 69.1%` · s1538 `538/941 = 57.2%` · the crossing commit `176268426` `541/1084 = 49.9%` · s2100 `541/1093 = 49.5%` · s2097 `541/1093`) (`git ls-tree <rev>:tasks` × that rev's own `goals.json`, matching `taskFile` EXACTLY): at s1538's tree it reproduces **538/941 = 57.2% to the digit**, at s1276's **527/763 = 69.1%** against a recorded 526/762 (±1, one boundary master). ⚠️ **At s2097's tree it yields 541/1093 where that fire recorded 532/1093** — denominator identical to the digit, numerator +9 — so s2097 almost certainly resolved leaves through `drain-block-check`'s SUBSTRING match, which matches more leaves and therefore reports fewer unregistered. **Both readings put the ratio below 50%, so the threshold verdict does not depend on which resolution is preferred**; the +9 is named here so the next fire re-measuring this does not mistake a method difference for a real jump. ⛔ **THAT "almost certainly" IS NOW MEASURED FALSE — REFUTED s2182 (F-2182-1), AND THE SENTENCE IS KEPT ONLY SO THE REFUTATION HAS A SUBJECT.** Replicating `drain-block-check`'s resolver EXACTLY (`:234–257` — `normalize()` then bidirectional substring, then the `leaf.id` fallback) at s2097's OWN tree yields **478/1093, not 532** — delta **63**, not 9. Two intermediate candidates miss it too: `normalize()`-equality **539**, `normalize()`+id-equality **536**. **No candidate method reproduces 532; its true derivation is UNRECOVERED**, and naming a mechanism for it was a guess wearing