nAssayBenchIfNearby` missing from the working tree while main sat at a365951 which contains it). When gating 031: diff working tree vs HEAD and REJECT any removal of committed code outside 031's firewall (SpriteAnimator/Balance.anim/entity transform site/new spec). If the office branch is missing from 031's final state: restore from HEAD (`git checkout HEAD -- src/game/Game.ts` then re-apply 031's legitimate hunks if any touched it) BEFORE committing, and write the finding.\012- Commit pending host-side edits (s51/s52 lock-clears + s9at/s9au bullets + tasks/031-033) if still uncommitted.\012- Drains pending: lane-a demo-profiles (intel banked in s51 line-1: bind-check gr.difficultyPreset.v1, crafting-fork likely empty); art-029's 19 raws (extract + contracts + LEDGER); then 031 (anim roundness code) / 032 (walk4 sheets) / 033 (crafting pipeline first run) outputs as the runner finishes them.\012- ⛔ **RETIRED s2405 (F-2405-1) — DO NOT RUN THAT `mv`: ITS NAMED SUBJECTS ARE GONE AND THE GLOB NOW AIMS AT AN ALREADY-SHIPPED MASTER.** The order read *"After the above: unpause `mv tasks/queue-paused/* tasks/queue/main/` (021/026/027/030), serial."* — and the parenthetical only LOOKS like a scope: the COMMAND is a glob, and a glob outlives the items it was written for. 📊 **MEASURED s2405: `tasks/queue-paused/` holds exactly ONE file and it is none of 021/026/027/030 — it is `s2382-PARKED-armed-duplicate-dispatch-lane-d-toolsurface-terrain-edge.md`, whose master `drain-block-check --queue` refuses as `⛔ ALREADY SHIPPED — DO NOT QUEUE` (leaf `status="merged"`, `mergeHash=0d718cead…`), and whose subject defect is verifiably CURED on main — `src/agent/ToolSurface.ts` no longer imports `world/Terrain` at all, and `:164` is the injected `options.buildTargetReachable ?? (() => true)` form the master prescribed.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, no fire ever ran it, this is NOT a false green, and the layered defences all held — the filename SELF-LABELS `PARKED`, the runner never reads `queue-paused` (0 references in `lane-runner-v3.sh`), and §2E already prescribes the `--queue` check that refuses in one second.** 🎯 **WHAT EARNS IT A CURE IS THE DIRECTION PLUS A LIVE, RECURRING TRIGGER: the destination is `tasks/queue/main/`, the runner dispatches whatever lands there with NO shipped-check of its own (its single `drain-block-check` mention is a COMMENT at `lane-runner-v3.sh:391` — verified by reading, not grepped), and §2E's independent trigger *"re-queue paused main items (queue-paused/) once the pile is below 2"* fires on EVERY dry board, today's included (pile 0). That is Mistake #8 — the 824k Flail, this catalog's most expensive recorded failure — one `mv` away, with a stale instruction pointing at it.** ➡️ **THE STANDING RULE THAT REPLACES IT: `queue-paused/` is NOT a resume queue, it is a PARKING LOT whose occupants change. Before moving anything out of it, run `node scripts/drain-block-check.mjs <master> --queue` and obey the verdict — the directory being non-empty is not evidence that its contents are owed.** ⓘ **The parked file is deliberately LEFT AS s2382 NAMED IT: it is untracked scratch, and renaming it would erase another fire's own labelling of its own finding (supersede, never erase).** 💡 **REUSABLE: a standing order that names its subjects in PROSE but selects them with a GLOB is two different instructions, and only the prose expires legibly. When you retire the last item a wildcard was written for, retire the wildcard in the same breath — otherwise it silently re-aims at whatever next occupies the directory, and the newcomer inherits an authority nobody granted it.**\012- Robin owes (nag politely in handoffs, never block on it): lane-d attempt-3 verdict (3a recommended), turret-feel + water-feel playtests, Mac full-regression evidence, favicon 16px eyeball.\012- Canon guardrails always: brief §9 (no firearms — frontier-tech only; illustrated never gory; no Native American enemies; naming per §9.4; the agent is "the Prospector").\012\012## GZ-01 + TK-01 DUTIES (added 2026-07-10, attended — the news pipeline goes live)\012ON EVERY REAL-CHANGE MERGE ON MAIN — **whoever landed it, not only the ones you drain** (the filter law is unchanged: the review names a player-visible change): APPEND a news item to marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md. 🔑 **RE-KEYED s1546 FROM THE DRAINER TO THE MERGE EVENT (F-1546-1).** The old wording read "every real-change merge **you drain**", which keys the duty on the AGENT — and the factory's drain load has moved to attended sessions, so the pipeline was simply never *entered* when a human drained. Measured: **four player-visible slices merged attended-side on the morning of 2026-08-08 (`99f0d60a40…` f-door-1, `38615d7841…` f-door-2, `5698e6ae30…` f-bal-1, `3dec093294…` mp-07b) — all four with review files, all four with ZERO news items**, while all twelve most-recent touches of the queue file were fires at drain time. Nothing in the pipeline was broken; the trigger just never fired. ➡️ **THEREFORE, AS A STANDING SWEEP: any fire backfills any real-change merge whose review exists and whose hash is absent from `gazette-queue.md`** (`grep` the hash — that is the whole check, and it costs one command). ⚠️ **BUT GREP THE 8-CHAR SHORT HASH ACROSS THE WHOLE OF `marketing/outbox/`, NEVER THE FULL HASH AGAINST `gazette-queue.md` ALONE — THE PIPELINE HAS TWO OWNER-FACING SINKS AND THE PRESCRIBED CHECK IS STRUCTURALLY BLIND TO ONE OF THEM (F-1600-1, measured s1600).** The daily TK-01 ticker digest below reaches the owner exactly as a GAZETTE item does, so a merge headlined there is REPORTED, not owed. 📐 **The two sinks cite hashes in DISJOINT conventions, which is what makes the blindness categorical rather than a sampling artifact — measured across the live outbox: ticker digests carry 618 short hashes and ZERO full-40 ones, while `gazette-queue.md` carries 86 full and 105 short.** A full-40 grep therefore *cannot* match a ticker digest in principle, no matter how many fires run it. 📊 **Cost of the narrow check, window 2026-08-05→s1600: 81 player-path-touching first-parent merges, of which the narrow check calls 47 ABSENT — 20 of those are headlined in a ticker digest and 1 sits in the gazette under its short hash, so 21 of 47 are FALSE POSITIVES (44.7%) and only 26 are genuinely unreported.** ⓘ **The damage is not wasted greps, it is an item that can never be discharged:** `3b2b33c29` ("the county's first standing — V4 Pro secures the-claim via the public door") was left as an UNJUDGED gazette candidate by s1599 and re-judged by s1600, when it had been headlined to the owner in `marketing/outbox/ticker-digest-2026-08-06.md:27` on 2026-08-07 — carrying its own OWNER CHOICE note at `marketing/outbox/ticker-digest-2026-08-06.md:58` — since before either fire existed. **A check that reports a discharged duty as owed reports it forever, and every fire pays the judgement cost again.** 💡 **THIS REPRICES ANY ABSENCE COUNT TAKEN THE NARROW WAY, INCLUDING THE ONE IN THE F-1599-1 CLAUSE ABOVE** — if ~45% of such a set is already published, the backlog it implies is smaller than it reads, and a cure sized against the raw figure is over-sized. Re-measure before building anything against it. 🔢 **AND DERIVE THE NEEDLE BY TRUNCATION, NEVER BY `%h` — `git log --format=%h` ABBREVIATES TO **9** CHARS IN THIS REPO, AND A 9-CHAR NEEDLE CANNOT MATCH AN 8-CHAR CITATION (F-1633-1, measured s1633).** git auto-abbreviates by object count, so `%h` silently grew past the 8 chars this clause prescribes; a fire that reads "grep the 8-char short hash", then obtains its candidates the obvious way, reproduces F-1600-1 **inside the very check written to cure it** — the method is right and the needle is wrong. 📊 **Measured s1633 over 63 player-path first-parent commits since 2026-08-05, same corpus, three needles: gazette-only 9-char → 14 absent · whole-outbox 9-char → 10 absent · whole-outbox 8-char → ZERO.** All 10 of