codex
The cache integration introduces a scene-transition race that can invalidate live textures, and the new tests cannot run under the production-preview harness. Four unit tests and the targeted asset-module typecheck passed.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Prevent stale scene requests from clearing the active atlas cache — /Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/worktrees/lane-d/src/assets/AssetLoading.ts:17-18
  When leaving an E2+ town while plaza props are loading, `TownTavernPilot.ts`’s `loadValid()` can retry an older variant after disposal. After `Game` resets the canvas to `'the claim'`, that late `'the town'` request enters this branch and closes the new run’s image bitmaps; its existing loaders then reject with `Shared atlas tracker disposed`. Resetting the cache can itself trigger the pending town load’s rejection and retry. Associate requests with their owning scene generation or cancel stale retries before allowing them to invalidate the current tracker.

- [P2] Separate source-injected tests from the production-preview suite — /Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/worktrees/lane-d/e2e/shared-atlas-dedupe.spec.ts:16-20
  `playwright.preview.config.ts` collects all eight cases, but the production bundle never requests `/src/game/Game.ts`, so this interception cannot install `__ATLAS_RUNTIME__`. The imported artifact helper also returns HTML under preview, which prevents these tests from completing. This breaks the documented production-suite command ([docs/DEPLOY.md:19](docs/DEPLOY.md#L19)). Give these dev-only tests an explicit harness boundary or provide instrumentation that also works with the production bundle.
